{"kind":"request","text":"CB-2: a press on a card control can lose its target, because each render replaces every child (builder diagnostic 676225fd, found by the E4 browser run at the Report press after Take). A member meets the same window at each background read. Keep unchanged controls in place across a render.","body":{"conditions":"Side lane after the E4, A1 and CR-2 head. (1) The render of the card browser (packages/mcp, browser/main.ts) keeps the element of a control whose label and state did not change. It replaces only what changed. (2) One browser case presses a control while a background read renders, and the press reaches its handler. A mutant that restores the full replacement fails that case. (3) The handoff of Report sends its message for the revision that the member saw, or the card states why not. Say what the host does with a message for an earlier revision today, and propose the rule if one is missing. (4) No new wait or deadline in a script. (5) The Card workflow passes at the head. One gate. Tell the planner before adoption if an identifier of an application changes.","target_head":"cfe769cebaa8a55a3ec9dff6e48238a304e2149a","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}